@ttyio Maybe if the scale is computed in fp16, some underflow?

Then it should just replace to `amax_sequeeze.to(torch.float32) / bound.to(torch.float32)`

Also, there is a typo, `amax_sequeeze` should likely be `amax_squeeze`

@vadimkantorov the fp16 onnx export is not supported in 2.1.3, we used gpu kernel to accelerate the fine-tuning so I point out the branch. 

Thank you for your suggesting we will continue improving the document.

For the float16 problem, TRT is weak typed, it does not matter what the output of gemm is fp32 or fp16, we use builder flag to allow fp16 kernel https://docs.nvidia.com/deeplearning/tensorrt/api/python_api/infer/Core/BuilderConfig.html#tensorrt.BuilderFlag
